## 11. Process sizing — [AGENT] (2026-09-14)

This rule permits brief or skipped stages when their responsibilities are satisfied or inapplicable. Record the reason or reused evidence; preserve this policy's scientific rules, owner rulings, source quarantine, executable gates, frozen record correctness, and runtime contracts. Existing verification can be reused when its revision, scope, and environment are still valid.

Where the goal layer is installed, review follows the installed goal runbook, § Review scope and evidence reuse. Without it, the rest of this paragraph is the review rule. New or reinterpreted equations/sources require a focused independent source/math check against original evidence. Ownership/interface changes and new modeling patterns require focused design review before implementation. Shared definition changes require consumer enumeration and checks, broadened if impact is unknown. Coupled architecture, multiple model families, or failed coverage require substantive independent integration review. Routine studies do not require stacked preflight critics, administrators, disposition critics, and round critics; use applicable evidence once. The main agent may execute directly and delegate scoped research or review with self-contained briefs.
